@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.api"

Feature: Zendesk Heat Score
	Testing for creating requests and viewing their heat scores

Setup:
	* I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                         |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1              |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp_cloud,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                             |
	| Shared Comments  | true                             |
	| SLA              | Gold                             |
	| Tier             | T4                               |
	| Support Region   | US                               |
	| Support Language | English                          |
	| External ID      | 12345678                         |

Teardown:
	* I teardown tickets requested by the users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Enduser1 |
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Enduser1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| 12345678 |

Scenario: View heat score of urgent priority request
	End users should be able to view the heat score on a urgent priority request.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                         |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb,liferay_dxp_cloud |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                         |
	| Role             | End-user                              |
	| Access           | Organization                          |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken   |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Vodafone UK Customer Portal           |
	| Language         | Portuguese                            |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                              | 
	| External ID      | Enduser1                              |
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" to an organization with organizationExternalId "83313192"
	And I create a DXP Cloud request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_cloud          |
	| Component                | backup_recovery                |
	| Liferay Version          | liferay_version_7_2            |
	| System Status            | production_completely_shutdown |
	| Subject                  | Request Heat Score Subject     |
	| Description              | Request Heat Score Description |
	| Organization External ID | 83313192                       |
    Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be given the priority level "urgent"
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken"
	And I change the sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "resolution_planning"
	And the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the sub-status "resolution_planning"
	And the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the environment "production"
	And the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the heat score "12"

Scenario: View heat score of high priority request
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	End users should be able to view the heat score on a high priority request.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Enduser1                      |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb,liferay_dxp_cloud |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                         |
	| Role             | End-user                              |
	| Access           | Organization                          |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken   |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1                   |
	| Language         | English                               |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)            |
	| External ID      | Enduser1                              |
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" to an organization with organizationExternalId "12345678"
	And I create a DXP Cloud request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_cloud                   |
	| Component                | connectivity                            |
	| Liferay Version          | liferay_version_7_2                     |
	| Tags                     | escalation_engineer                     |
	| System Status            | production_severely_impacted_inoperable |
	| Subject                  | Request Heat Score Subject              |
	| Description              | Request Heat Score Description          |
	| Organization External ID | 12345678                                |
    Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be given the priority level "high"
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken"
	And I change the sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "resolution_planning"
	And the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the sub-status "resolution_planning"
	And the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the environment "production"
	And the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the heat score "10"

