Scenario: Update a ticket status to solved and view heat score after subsequent updates
	Testing the update of a ticket status to solved and view heat score. 

    Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Enduser1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb                 |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                       |
	| Role             | End-user                            |
	| Access           | Organization                        |
	| Email            | zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                   |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1                 |
	| Language         | English                             |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)          |
	| External ID      | Enduser1                            |
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" to an organization with organizationExternalId "12345678"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_4                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Heat Score Subject                       |
	| Description              | Request Heat Score Description                   |
	| Organization External ID | 12345678                                         |
    Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be given the priority level "normal"
	When I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.enduser1@zendesk.com.broken"
	And I change the sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "resolution_planning"
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the sub-status "resolution_planning"
	And the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the environment "production"
	And the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the heat score "6"
	When I change the status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "solved"
	And I change the sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "solution_proposed"
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "solved"
	And the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the heat score "6"

